From ed023979be0a52fe4965a342df5cc6d45a7c379e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kris Williams <115474+kriswill@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 15:32:06 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(ui): ansi command entries in the tab bar

Adds argv and ansi fields to ui.tab_bar_right command entries. argv runs
the program directly without a shell; ansi = true preserves SGR styling
from the command's last stdout line and renders it inline, stripping all
other escape sequences. Status commands receive the focused workspace's
metadata tokens as HERDR_TOKEN_<NAME> environment variables and re-run
when those tokens change, so an external status producer like dotbar
owns presentation without polling lag.

Rebased onto v0.9.0, where the tab bar is rendered by the client from a
server snapshot. Styled output now travels as an optional `spans` list
on the tab status segment (packed fg/bg colors plus modifier bits) with
`text` kept as the unstyled fallback, and the client tab bar renders the
spans over the theme base style. The private protocol version is bumped
to 23 because the snapshot's bincode layout changed after 22 shipped in
v0.9.0; the generated API schema artifact is regenerated to match.
